# Implementation Plan: Base44 Cognitive Optimization

This plan focuses on refining the Base44/Antigravity integration in the primary `appforge-main` project, leveraging the new Gemini 3 core for more efficient "quantum channel" communication.

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> This optimization will use Gemini 3 to "compress" prompts sent via Base44 to reduce latency and improve signal quality.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component: Antigravity LLM Provider]

#### [MODIFY] [llm.ts](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/swarm/core/llm.ts)
- Implement **Semantic Compression** logic using `geminiAdapter`.
- Pre-process large prompts ( > 1000 tokens) to summarize context before sending via the Base44 AuditLog.
- Standardize signal statuses and logging patterns.

### [Component: Cloud Bridge Monitoring]

#### [MODIFY] [base44.ts](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/swarm/tools/base44.ts)
- Add a `checkHealth()` method to verify API connectivity and authorization.
- Implement a **Quantum Heartbeat** to log bridge status periodically.

#### [MODIFY] [swarm_telemetry_server.ts](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/scripts/swarm_telemetry_server.ts)
- Integrate Base44 health status into the telemetry dashboard.
- Alert the Command Center if the cloud bridge is offline.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification
- Run `scripts/benchmark_base44.ts` (NEW) to measure signal compression ratios and latency.

### Manual Verification
- Observe the "Bridge Status" in the Oracle Command Center UI.
- Verify that large prompts are correctly summarized in the `AuditLog` metadata.
